WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Praise becomes direct address. Follow the proposed correspondences around the prayer at 1:5.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
5 thematic movements in this study arrangement. The labels summarize passages; they are not Quran translations.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Read the opening praise beside the closing description of human paths. This study map proposes a thematic relation, rather than repeated wording.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The Day of Judgment and the request for guidance bring destiny and the path toward it into conversation.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
At 1:5, the address changes from speaking about God to speaking directly to Him. Worship and asking for help meet in one verse.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The connecting marks gather into nested rings. Their symmetry visualizes this reading; it does not establish the reading by itself.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Read the prayer again: how does its direct address change the way you hear the opening praise?
